From 513854e6158673cdb7170ea92204728d9b50b2ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:04:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hedging, and the shops that had been charging their own
 buying price

The formal garden's perimeter is two hotspots on the same twenty tiles, not one. Fencing sits on
the wall boundary; Hedging stands on the tile, so a garden can have both, which is what OSRS does.
The fence shipped with the formal garden round. This is the hedge - seven tiers, 56 to 80, three
pieces each over the same twenty tiles, and the last unclaimed hotspot in that room.

WHICH PIECE GOES ON WHICH TILE is named rather than assumed. Three Hedging hotspots are placed and
their ghosts are two straights and a corner; the thorny hedge's own three models ARE those three
ghosts, vertex for vertex and box for box, which is what says a tier's triple in poh.loc is
ordered (straight, corner, straight). Two tiers prove it twice: the small box and tall box hedges
are one model set at two heights, and so are the fancy and tall fancy, and both pairs come out
small-then-tall under the file order, which is also the level order. tools/genhedge.py re-derives
all of that and refuses to write if any of it stops holding.

THE SHOPS WERE WRONG, AND HAD BEEN SINCE THEY WERE BUILT. Going to the wiki for the hedge levels
turned up the real shop rows, and a shop row has a sell column and a buy column:

                       charged      OSRS charges
    Limestone brick         10                26
    Marble block       125,000           325,000
    Gold leaf          130,000           130,000   (right by coincidence)
    Magic stone      4,000,000           975,000
    Bagged dead tree       400             1,000

^poh_stone_sell was 500 - the ratio the Stonemason BUYS at - and ^poh_garden_sell was 400, the same
mistake at the Garden Centre. Every item's cache cost had then been inflated to make the wrong
multiplier produce the buy-back price, so three places agreed with each other and all three were
wrong, and the batteries agreed too because their "OSRS price" tables were the buy column. The
multipliers are 1300 and 1000 now, the costs are the cache's own values, and both batteries read
the sell column.

THE MAGIC STONE IS MINE. It went in yesterday with the costume room's cape rack at 4,000,000,
written from memory rather than read, asserted in the commit message, the project doc and a battery
check that compared it against itself. It is 750,000, he sells it for 975,000 and he stocks ten.
Same class of mistake as the five wrong obj names in the cave horror drop table, and the same
answer: read the row.

AND SIX THINGS WERE BUILDABLE AND UNOBTAINABLE. The formal garden's flowerbeds cost a bagged
flower and nothing in the game sold one - the comment in poh_garden.inv explaining why the flowers
were left out had gone stale the day the formal garden round wired the hotspots. They are stocked
now, with the seven new bagged hedges, which needed no import: every bagged anything in OSRS is the
same sack model this repo already has.

Battery group 63 is the general form of that bug. Every obj any family names as a material is
either stocked by a shop in this repo, or is in a table naming the script that makes it - and that
script has to mention it, so a plank nobody mills goes red the same as a flower nobody sells. 37
materials, 29 bought, 8 made.

Two tools came out of it:

  - tools/poh_mutate_spec.py. A mutation to furnspec.json cannot be tested by poh_mutate.py: the
    battery re-runs the generators in place, so group 38 goes red first whatever the edit was, and
    the check under test never fires. This edits the spec, regenerates, and only then runs the
    battery - the sequence a person would actually produce. It is what proves the unobtainable
    check fires on its own rather than behind something else.
  - the dead-click audit was only counting locs named at a loc_add call, so the rugs, the combat
    ring, the chapel windows and now the hedge - everything that picks its loc through a proc -
    were invisible to it. 327 locs became 448, and none of the 121 was a dead click.

Dead Build ops in a house: 32 -> 29. Every hotspot the formal garden places is claimed. What is
left needs a dungeon or a second storey.

